   "id": "event-9",
   "kindId": "event",
   "name": "Event 9 — The Undercroft",
   "aliases": [
    "The Undercroft"
   ],
   "tags": [
    "past"
   ],
   "status": "canon",
   "summary": "Played entirely inside the Crimson Vale. Players recover the five tombs and gather the evidence to clear Obeah of the Oathbreaker title.",
   "body": "By interacting with encounters at Event 9, PCs should come to understand: that Obeah's realm is a shadow of its former self, straining to keep out oblivion; that Obeah did not earn the title of Oathbreaker and must right this wrong; and that they need the five coffins to conduct the Rite of Aeons at Event 10.",
   "occursAt": "Event 9",
   "sources": [
    {
     "label": "Event 9 Synopsis & Definitions"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "event-10",
   "kindId": "event",
   "name": "Event 10 — The End",
   "aliases": [
    "The End"
   ],
   "tags": [
    "upcoming"
   ],
   "status": "draft",
   "summary": "Players return to a Mystvale six months into a losing war, and either enact or sabotage the Rite of Aeons.",
   "body": "Mystvale is a final redoubt. Oblivion has claimed the aetheric Wells at the leyline intersections and uses them to summon an avatar for each of the Unbound. The site divides into safe, grey and nether zones; the Rite must be performed at dusk on Saturday.",
   "occursAt": "Event 10",
   "sources": [
    {
     "label": "Event 10 — The End Design Doc"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "rite-of-aeons",
